Lizzy: It's okay. You're okay.


Juniper: I don't know where to begin.
join Barb right [animation="Slide From Right" wait="true"]
Barb: How about with why you forced us into a time loop?
join "Lady MacDeath" rightmost [animation="Slide In Up" wait="true"]
"Lady MacDeath": Yes. Seconded.
Juniper: Okay, so, this is going to sound crazy. This wasn't actually a time loop.
Everyone: ...
Juniper: There's this TV show called Lizzy Springs Monster Hunter and Werewolf, and it ran for two seasons from the years 2000- 2002.
Everyone: ...
Lizzy: Juniper..
Lizzy: Are you saying someone stole my life story and is making money off it?
Juniper: No. No. I practised this conversation so many times... Okay.
Juniper: What I meant to say is, we've all been under a lot of pressure from the vampire lords, and I had this vision where Vermilion Hills was destroyed. I told Valerie.
Valerie: Yes, I remember that.
Juniper: What I didn't tell you Valerie was that in one of my visions, Lizzy died.
Lizzy: Oh...
Juniper: I didn’t tell anyone, because I wasn't going to let it happen.
When my family first moved to Vermilion Hills, it was said the silver made their Clairvoyance stronger. I decided to test the theory by going into the mine, to just widen the picture a bit. See if I could prevent it.
Well, the silver was too much. I saw something... not of this world.
Juniper: We are in a TV show, and we only exist for 2 seasons and 22 episodes.
Juniper: Ever wonder why weird things happen on a weekly basis?
Lizzy: I don't believe this.
Juniper: In my vision, I saw that we don't get a season 3. Season 2 ends on a cliff hanger. A cliff hanger where you're presumed dead, Lizzy.
Lizzy: I don't understand…
Juniper: The day we've been living over and over again is season 2, episode 21\: Lady in Waiting.  Tomorrow would've been season 2, episode 22\: One in Vermilion.
Valerie: The final episode of the show.
Lizzy: They named it a stupid pun? No wonder it got canceled.
Juniper: I'll be honest, the titles grew on me eventually.
Juniper: I chose episode 21 because it's the only episode where we can spend time with each other. I tried earlier ones but they weren't the same.
Barb: Why didn't you try to change the ending of the final episode? Also
Barb: just double checking, we're okay with this whole we're a tv show thing?
Noah: Yeah.
Dagger: I don’t really know what a tv show is, but I assume it's those watchies?
Lizzy: Please stop showing your age.
Juniper: Oh, I tried. I tried a lot. The first year was me trying and trying and trying but no matter what we just stopped existing. Even if I saved Lizzy.
Valerie: The first year?
Lizzy: We've been looping for a year???
Juniper: ...
Juniper: More like.
Juniper: Twenty-five or so years. Give or take.
Barb: No.
Noah: Wait I can legally drink now?
Valerie: Twenty five years. .. that's unimaginable. How are you not.. well...
Juniper: Insane?
Juniper: I'll be honest, having visions was already like reliving the same day. At first, when I set up the automatic rewind, I would do everything exactly as it was supposed to be. Sometimes I would spice things up again and spend time with each and every one of you. I know so much about Barb's love of bad Sci Fi monster of the week shows and her crush on Lizzy-
Lizzy: Wait
Barb: Hold on um sorry what
Dagger: what
Lady Knightmare\: Huzzah! What a twist!
Noah: I knew it.
Juniper: Oh. Sorry Barb. I. I'm still used to nothing really sticking after the reset.
Barb: You are so mean! All of you stop smirking!
Lizzy: Awh... you're so flustered.
Barb: UGH!!!
Juniper: I was comfortable in knowing exactly how everyone would react to everything. What would happen every second. It was safe.
Valerie: Did you ever let the episode end? Episode 22?
Juniper: There's nothing. I saw it. In my vision.
Juniper: If it ends, I won't be able to rewind.
Lizzy: Well. We don't know what will happen. Not really.
Juniper: But my visions..
Lizzy: They've been wrong before.